<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 51,357 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 51,357 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 51,357 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 44,090 tonnes on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			23,433	    26,636</p>
<p>    Import cargo			27,924	    17,454</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight ships were expected to sail and 13 were expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    73,000	 Chesapeak City    18/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-1	   18/2</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Keefan		17/2</p>
<p>Crude oil		72,944	 Johar		 18/2</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Warbah		 due</p>
<p>Sulphur		   3,900	 Sea Princess	 due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
